# PLAN-862 entry-unit source profile — ACE M1 corpus rows U01..U10.
#
# One source x the AV entry-unit profile (and the scalar control on the same
# bytes where the old path is the point). Every expectation here is an
# INDEPENDENT, hand-computed oracle (T-02 entry-contract §2/§4/§6), not a
# snapshot of what the pipeline happened to print:
#
#   U01  int entry: `return 42` on the value channel (and the scalar control
#        on the SAME bytes, exit 42 — the old path does not move)
#   U02  Unit entry: the channel is `unit`, NEVER an i32 0
#   U03  script tail: twice(21) = 42 through the synthetic entry
#   U04  script without a tail: the Unit channel
#   U05  1/0 is a trap, not a value and not an error completion
#   U06  no entry at all                      -> source.entry-missing
#   U07  an entry with parameters             -> source.entry-params
#   U08  a Unit entry returning a value       -> source.unit-return-value
#   U09  an expression statement in an int fn -> source.entry-tail
#   U10  a second `main`                      -> source.entry-duplicate
#
# The scalar checks (`av-scalar-*`) are the ZERO-DRIFT control: the old
# profile still accepts the int entry byte-for-byte and still REJECTS the
# new forms (settle: `source.unsupported`), so the new surface is never a
# silent widening of the old one.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.u01"
  tags: ["ace-m1", "entry-unit", "value"]
  links: ["PLAN-862"]
  source: { file: "src/U01.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "av", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: { recipe: "ac-av/core-run-v1", av: { entry: "d_main", profile: "entry-unit" }, steps: [{ op: "run" }] },
      expect: { completion: "success", av_channel: "value", exit: 42 } },
    { id: "av-scalar-control", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: { recipe: "ac-av/core-run-v1", av: { entry: "d_main" }, steps: [{ op: "run" }] },
      expect: { completion: "success", exit: 42 } }
  ]
}
```

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.u02"
